{"diagnosis": "TRAP: fetch misalign addr low bits nonzero with tohost FAIL 0xdead because mem_la_addr low bits are 2'b10 instead of expected 2'b00 for word-aligned fetch. Root cause at picorv32.v:382 where mem_la_addr forces {next_pc[31:2]+mem_la_firstword_xfer,2'b10} for mem_do_prefetch/mem_do_rinst and {reg_op1[31:2],2'b10} for data. Every lookahead fetch therefore stays misaligned and never makes progress.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -379,4 +379,4 @@
 	assign mem_la_write = resetn && !mem_state && mem_do_wdata;
 	assign mem_la_read = resetn && ((!mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word && !mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rdata)) ||
 			(COMPRESSED_ISA && mem_xfer && (!last_mem_valid ? mem_la_firstword : mem_la_firstword_reg) && !mem_la_secondword && &mem_rdata_latched[1:0]));
-	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b10} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b10};
+	assign mem_la_addr = (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst) ? {next_pc[31:2] + mem_la_firstword_xfer, 2'b00} : {reg_op1[31:2], 2'b00};", "expected": "tohost PASS (no FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: fetch misalign, mem_la_addr[1:0]==2'b00"}

